Snickersnee comes from _The Mikado_, by Gilbert and Sullivan.  I do not
think that "silliness" is a good reason to remove a feature from Nethack;
silliness is part and parcel of what makes Nethack so great. (Besides,
this is a game about going down a hole in the ground to kill things and
take their stuff, in which a doorway can accommodate 742 soldier corpses,
917 suits of plate mail, and 693 halberds, but only one newt.  Complaining
about Snickersnee being silly in such circumstances seems to miss the
point :)

I don't use Snickersnee unless I get it very early, because Samurai are
lawful, long swords are not difficult to obtain, and there are several
guaranteed fountains in the early game, but I'd still miss it.
